ment to advancing knowledge in oncology and surgical outcomes.", "CHEN L:Chen L is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation techniques.", "BHATT AD:Bhatt AD is a researcher who has studied the impact of electrical stimulation on dysphagia in patients with head and neck cancer.", "GOODWIN N:Goodwin N is a researcher contributing to studies on dysphagia and its treatments.", "CASH E:Cash E is a researcher involved in studies related to dysphagia.", "BHATT G:Bhatt G is a researcher who has worked on studies related to dysphagia treatments.", "SILVERMAN CL:Silverman CL is a researcher contributing to studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation.", "SPANOS WJ:Spanos WJ is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and its treatments.)<|COMPLETE|>", "UFDOF:The Functional Unit of Oropharyngeal Dysphagia (UFDOF), also known as Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea, is a specialized unit located within HUPA (Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias) in the Community of Madrid. This unit is dedicated to the evaluation, diagnosis, and treatment of patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. In addition to providing direct patient care, UFDOF is committed to training healthcare professionals to enhance the quality of care for individuals with dysphagia. Through its focused approach, UFDOF aims to improve the management of swallowing disorders and ensure comprehensive support for affected patients.", "JAPANESE SOCIETY OF DYSPHAGIA REHABILITATION:The Japanese Society of Dysphagia Rehabilitation (JSDR) is an organization that advocates for a transdisciplinary approach in the rehabilitation of dysphagia.", "LOGOPEDIA:Logopedia refers to the field of speech therapy that encompasses services aimed at the treatment of dysphagia, a condition that affects an individual's ability to swallow. It plays a crucial role in the rehabilitation of patients suffering from this disorder, providing essential support and therapeutic interventions to improve their swallowing capabilities and overall communication skills.", "TERAPIA OCUPACIONAL:Terapia Ocupacional (Occupational Therapy) is a discipline that plays a significant role in the rehabilitation of patients with dysphagia. The Terapia Ocupacional service specifically focuses on assisting these patients in their recovery process, utilizing various therapeutic techniques to improve their swallowing abilities and overall quality of life.", "ENFERMERÍA:Enfermería (Nursing) provides essential support in the care of patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects the ability to swallow. The nursing staff plays a crucial role in assessing patients and implementing dietary modifications as part of the treatment for swallowing disorders. Specifically, the nursing team is instrumental in the assessment and care of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia within the hospital setting. Their expertise and interventions are vital for ensuring the well-being and recovery of these patients.", "NEURÓLOGOS:Neurólogos (Neurologists) are specialists involved in the assessment and treatment of dysphagia-related conditions.", "DIETISTAS AMERICANAS:Dietistas Americanas, or American Dietitians, are professionals who offer dietary advice and support specifically for patients experiencing dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}